Description: Simulates multivariate normal data from Gaussian graphical models
    (GGMs) with realistic psychometric network structure. Networks can be
    generated with stochastic block model or small-world (Watts-Strogatz)
    topologies (Christensen & Choi, 2026 <doi:10.1037/met0000853>;
    Christensen, Choi, Yang, & Xue, 2026 <doi:10.48550/arXiv.2609.05678>),
    with edge weight distributions calibrated to empirical psychometric
    networks (Huth et al., 2025 <doi:10.1038/s41562-025-02314-2>). Additional tools include
    small-world network metrics, a proximity-swap ring lattice construction
    algorithm, categorization of continuous data with skew, and the addition
    of population (model) error so that the true network fits at a target
    level of a fit index (CFI, TLI, RMSEA, or SRMR) using the methods of
    Cudeck and Browne (1992) <doi:10.1007/BF02295424>, Tucker, Koopman, and
    Linn (1969) <doi:10.1007/BF02290601>, Wu and Browne (2015)
    <doi:10.1007/s11336-015-9451-3>, or Hu and Bentler (1998)
    <doi:10.1037/1082-989X.3.4.424>.
